{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01WB7JQ4Sb71BneYdFRjxSSb", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://carnegieendowment.org/research/2022/03/the-peculiar-case-of-the-pakistan-peoples-party-as-an-opposition-party\"}, {\"url\": \"https://carnegieendowment.org/research/2022/03/the-peculiar-case-of-the-pakistan-peoples-party-as-an-opposition-party?lang=en\"}, {\"url\": \"https://newageislam.com/current-affairs/pti-ready-role-opposition-party/d/11530\"}, {\"url\": \"https://carnegieendowment.org/2022/03/07/peculiar-case-of-pakistan-peoples-party-as-opposition-party-pub-86568\"}, {\"url\": \"https://carnegieendowment.org/publications/86568\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.dawn.com/news/1404648\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.ecoi.net/en/file/local/1043272/1997_1300196059_pak30203.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://s.thepeninsula.qa/article/24/05/2013/sharif-faces-100-strong-opposition\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.thenews.pk/tns/detail/963114-ppp-returns-to-the-centre-stage\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:41:00.835Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Pakistan People's Party emerged as leading opposition party times national level", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_015pbCCtDERTQ63MvoFiZcn8", "content": [{"title": "• Research", "url": "https://carnegieendowment.org/research/2022/03/the-peculiar-case-of-the-pakistan-peoples-party-as-an-opposition-party"}, {"title": "• Research", "url": "https://carnegieendowment.org/research/2022/03/the-peculiar-case-of-the-pakistan-peoples-party-as-an-opposition-party?lang=en"}, {"title": "New Age Islam", "url": "https://newageislam.com/current-affairs/pti-ready-role-opposition-party/d/11530"}, {"title": "• Research", "url": "https://carnegieendowment.org/2022/03/07/peculiar-case-of-pakistan-peoples-party-as-opposition-party-pub-86568"}, {"title": "carnegieendowment.org", "url": "https://carnegieendowment.org/publications/86568"}, {"title": "Pakistan Peoples Party", "url": "https://www.dawn.com/news/1404648"}, {"title": "1997 1300196059 pak30203", "url": "https://www.ecoi.net/en/file/local/1043272/1997_1300196059_pak30203.pdf"}, {"title": "CHAIRMAN: DR. KHALID BIN THANI AL THANI", "url": "https://s.thepeninsula.qa/article/24/05/2013/sharif-faces-100-strong-opposition"}, {"title": "PPP returns to the Centre stage", "url": "https://www.thenews.pk/tns/detail/963114-ppp-returns-to-the-centre-stage"}]}, "The search turned up several sources, but most are dated, and the most recent ones show the PPP in a government role rather than opposition.\n\n- **2013 election:** Dawn's party summary says the PPP became the largest opposition party in the National Assembly, though it won a majority and formed the government in Sindh. The Peninsula's pre-election analysis had predicted it would be the single largest bloc in the opposition with about 40 MPs.\n- **2018–2022 opposition:** The News reports that with 56 seats in the current National Assembly, the PPP played a pivotal role in the opposition to the PTI government.\n- **Role since then:** Carnegie notes that the PPP has not been in power at the federal level since 2013, but it has governed Sindh throughout. Per The News, the party later returned to power in Islamabad as part of a ruling coalition after the PTI government fell in April 2022.\n- **Older precedent:** A 1997 International Crisis Group note describes the PPP as \"the largest single opposition party\" in the Punjab, which is a provincial rather than national claim.\n\nI didn't find a source confirming a current (2026) national opposition ranking, so the 2013 and 2018–2022 periods are the best-supported examples. The search results don't say what the PPP's current position is."], "durationSeconds": 6.657087083, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01WB7JQ4Sb71BneYdFRjxSSb", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
